  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH PROJECT IN RESPONSE TO THE CONFLICT EMERGENCY IN MACOMIA DISTRICT, CABO DELGADO PROVINCE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe PRONANAC EDUCATIONAL is committed to providing safe and sustainable solutions in the area of Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH), focusing on resettlement centers in the Macomia district, northern Mozambique. The project is implemented in close collaboration with local government and humanitarian partners, aligning with the WASH Cluster and national humanitarian response plans. The activities include: rehabilitation of manual water points, ensuring access to safe water construction of family latrines, with integrated units for menstrual hygiene construction of emergency latrines in critical contexts promotion of community hygiene, with an emphasis on training on good practices and approaches such as CLTS active community engagement, involving internally displaced persons, returnees, and host communities and partnerships with local artisans, fostering the development of local capacities and context-adapted solutions. The project aims to ensure that populations affected by conflict and displacement have dignified, inclusive, and equitable access to essential WASH services, contributing to the reduction of public health risks and the improvement of overall well-being and resilience in fragile settings.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
